    \centering
    \includegraphics[width=\textwidth]{Fig10.png}
    \caption{Accumulated melt production over a 4.5 Gyr time interval based on the lunar impactor flux. Here the accumulated melt volume $V_M$, its conversion into a uniform magma ocean depth and the melt volume normalized by the planet volume $V_\mathrm{M}/V_\mathrm{P}$ are plotted. In the bars, different color shading separated by black lines indicates the melt production accumulated over the full 4.5 Gyr and smaller time intervals, as indicated for a Moon-size planet in the upper left panel.}
    \label{fig:melt-pl-size-total}
