\begin{proof}[Proof of Lemma~\ref{lm:inequalities}]

	Part (a).
	Follows from computing the norms of the individual pieces of $\mathcal{R}$, and using $r$ and$ c$ are of the same asymptotic order by Assumption~\ref{ass:reg.cond}.

	Part (b). Let $\bar{d}$ denote the largest diagonal value of $L=B'B$. We have
	\begin{equation}
		\begin{aligned}[b]
			||B|| = \bar{\rho} (L) 
			=
			\bar{\rho}(D^{-1/2}LD^{-1/2}\cdot D)
			\leq
			\bar{\rho}(D^{-1/2}LD^{-1/2})
