\subsection{Organization of the paper} The paper is structured as follows: Section~\ref{Sec:pre} covers preliminaries, including the Novikov ring, non-Archimedean normed spaces, big quantum homology, deformed Floer homology and PSS isomorphisms. Sectionetc~\ref{Sec:spec} develops deformed Hamiltonian spectral invariants and proves the key Ljusternik-Schnirelman inequality. Section~\ref{sec:gw} establishes critical links between nonvanishing Gromov-Witten invariants and spectral invariant behavior. Section~\ref{sec:mainpf} provides the proofs for the main Theorems~\ref{thm:mainthm}--\ref{thm:onept} on degenetate symplectic fixed point estimates. Appendices~\ref{sec:coadjoint} and~\ref{Sec:toric} apply the theory to coadjoint orbits of compact simple Lie groups and symplectic toric manifolds, respectively.



