\subsection{Simulation details}
To perform the dynamics, we followed the same procedure used for MD simulations of molecules/particle systems~\cite{Grassmann2024}: we first generate a system with a nucleus in random positions inside a squared box of edge $L=\sqrt{N}$ with periodic boundary conditions (to obtain them with replicate the system in every direction). Next,  each simulation has been carried on for a total time of $10^4$, integrating equations of motions with a time step of $10^{-3}$. Forces are evaluated as done in Miotto~\textit{et al.}~\cite{voronoi2024}.




