\section{Discussion}\label{sec:discussion}
We now proceed to discuss some implications of our attack.
First, we begin with a discussion of how the detectability threshold $\eta$ might be estimated in practice as well as discuss the detectability and profit tradeoff.
Next, we expound on why such attacks can be particularly problematic for both users in the blockchain, as well as protocol designers as these attacks are, at least in theory, difficult to prevent. 
Furthermore, despite the supposed rational nature of the attack as evident in our game theoretic analysis in~\Cref{sec:analysis}, as well as the difficulty of attack prevention, we have not yet observed such attacks in practice. We therefore also outline some plausible explanations as to why this is so.

