\section{Conclusion}
We have proposed a Peaceman-Rachford-based time domain decomposition method for optimal control of hyperbolic PDEs. To this end, we formulated the optimality system as a sum of two maximally dissipative operators that may be interpreted as serial coupling of optimality systems. This allowed us to show convergence of the corresponding Peaceman-Rachford iteration in function space. We illustrated the method by means of two numerical examples involving a wave equation in two space dimensions and a heat equation in three space dimensions.



