\section{Wave breaking-induced dissipation}\label{sec:diss}
%
In this section, we discuss the turbulence dissipation induced by wave breaking. First, in section~\ref{sec:b_param}, we confirm that the dissipation caused by wave breaking is controlled by the wave slope at breaking and is quantified by the inertial scaling originally proposed by \cite{drazen2008inertial}. Next, in section~\ref{sec:prof}, we analyze the vertical profiles at different stages of the wave field and demonstrate that wave breaking promotes a transition to turbulence, with $\langle\varepsilon\rangle(z)\propto z^{-1}$, and demonstrate that the inertial scaling argument for the dissipation due to breaking can be used to unify the dissipation profiles at different $u_\ast/c$. 
%
