	\noindent{\bf Organization of the paper}: In Section \ref{prelims}, we recall basic results on hyperbolic geodesic metric spaces and their (Gromov) boundaries, and define the Cannon--Thurston map. In Subsection \ref{subsec-qi emb of T3}, we prove Theorem \ref{thm-emb of T31}, which serves as a key ingredient in the proof of Theorem \ref{thm-bary imp expo growth1}. The latter is proved in Subsection \ref{subsec-expo growth}.

	\noindent Section \ref{metric graph bundle sec} reviews relevant results on metric graph bundles from \cite{pranab-mahan}. Following \cite[Proposition $6.6$]{ps-krishna}, we provide a detailed description of the boundary of a metric graph bundle over $[0,\infty)$ in Proposition \ref{description of pa X}.

	\noindent In Section \ref{sec-main theorems over rays}, we prove our main theorems. Subsections \ref{sec-main one-ended over ray}, \ref{main thm over ray graph gen sec}, and \ref{applications over ray sec} contain the proofs of Theorems \ref{thm-combo1} $(B)$, \ref{main thm over ray graph gen}, and \ref{thm-combo1} $(A)$, respectively (along with Corollary \ref{cor-main group over ray}). Notably, Theorem \ref{main thm over ray graph gen} is the main step towards proving Theorem \ref{thm-combo1} $(A)$.

