		\noindent\underline{Induction hypothesis}: Suppose that we have defined $\phi_n:B(v_0,n)\map X$ where $n\ge1$. Let $\phi_n(w_i)=x_i$ for all $i\in\{1,\cdots,l\}$. Let $w'_i\in V(B(v_0,n))$ be the adjacent vertex to $w_i$ for all $i\in\{1,\cdots,l\}$. (Note that for any $w'_i$ there exists exactly one $j\ne i$ such that $w'_i=w'_j$. For ease of exposition, we are not making this distinction.) Let $\phi_n(w'_i)=x'_i$ for all $i\in\{1,\cdots,l\}$. Then we have the following.
