		Moreover, $\phi(u)\ne\phi(v)$ for all distinct vertices $u, v\in V(T_3)$. Indeed, let $u,v\in B(v_0,n)$ for some $n\in\N$. If $\phi(u)=\phi(v)$ then $\phi_n(u)=\phi_n(v)$, and by the above inequality $(*)$, we have $\frac{1}{K}D-K\le\frac{1}{K}d_{T_3}(u,v)-K\le 0$, and so $D\le K^2$ $-$ contradicting to the choice of $D$. This completes the proof of $(1)$.


