			Applying Claim to $p_2$ and $p_3$, by abusing notation, we have $\eta_2,\eta_3\in\pa X$ such that $max\{(\eta_2,\xi_2)_{p_2}, (\eta_2,x_0)_{p_2}, (\eta_3,\xi_3)_{p_3},(\eta_3,x_0)_{p_3}\}\le D_{\ref{lem-small inner prod}}(\dl,K)$.


			Let $S(v_0,1)=\{v_1,v_2,v_3\}$. Note that $S(v_0,1)\sse\G_0$. Suppose $\G_1$ are the union of fixed three geodesic rays in $T_3$ starting from $v_i$'s such that $\G_0\cap\G_1=S(v_0,1)$. Define $\phi_1:S(v_0,1)\cup\G_1\map X$ sending $v_i\mapsto p_i$ and geodesic ray of $\G'_1$ that strat at $v_i$ to the geodesic ray $[p_i,\eta_i)$.

			By our choice of $D$, $d(\phi_0(v_0),\phi_1(v_i))> R_{\ref{D-barycenter}}(\dl,D_{\ref{barycenter}}(\dl)+L)$, and so no two of $\{\phi_0(v_0),\phi_1(v_i):i=1,2,3\}$ are $(D_{\ref{barycenter}}(\dl)+L)$-barycenter of an ideal triangle.

			{\em Claim} 2: $(\eta_1,\eta_2,\eta_3)\in\pa^3X$ and $\{\eta_1,\eta_2,\eta_3\}\cap\{\xi_1,\xi_2,\xi_3\}=\emptyset$.

			{\em Proof of Claim} 2: Let us first show that $\eta_1\notin\{\xi_1,\xi_2,\xi_3\}$. Now by Lemma \ref{local to global}, the arclength parametrization of $[q_1,p_1]\cup[p_1,p'_1]$ is a $K'$-quasigeodesic, where $K'=K_{\ref{local to global}}(\dl,D_{\ref{lem-small inner prod}}(\dl,K))$. Since $p'_1\in[x_0,\xi_1)\cap[p_1,\xi_1)$ and $q_1\in[p_1,\eta_1)$ was arbitrary, so the arclength parametrization of $(\xi_1,p_1]\cup[p_1,\eta_1)$ is $K'$-quasigeodesic. Again for any $x\in[x_0,\xi_l],~l=2,3$, $(p_1,x)_{x_0}\le D_{\ref{lem-small inner prod}}(\dl,K)$ (since $[p_1,x_0]\cup[x_0,\xi_l)$ is $K$-quasigeodesic). So by Lemma \ref{local to global}, the arclength parametrization of $(\eta_1,p_1]\cup[p_1,x_0]\cup[x_0,\xi_l],~l=2,3$ is $K'$-quasigeodesic. Hence $\eta_1\notin\{\xi_1,\xi_2,\xi_3\}$.	


			By similar argument as above, we can conclude that $\eta_2,\eta_3\notin\{\xi_1,\xi_2,\xi_3\}$. Now by Lemma \ref{local to global}, $(\eta_i,p_i]\cup[p_i,x_0]\cup[x_0,\eta_{i\pm1})$ is also a $K'$-quasigeodesic for any $i\in\{1,2,3\}$. Therefore, $(\eta_1,\eta_2,\eta_3)\notin\pa^3X$. So Claim 2 is proved.

			{\bf Step 3}: Next, we will take points on geodesic rays $[p_i,\xi_i)$ and $[p_i,\eta_i)$ where $i\in\{1,2,3\}$ that are at a distance $D$ from $p_i$. Like in Step 1, we will find geodesic rays starting from those points such that arclength parametrization of the concatenation of these geodesic rays with the existing qi embedding is also $K'$-qi embedding.

			Inductively, we will get a $K'$-qi embedding $\phi=\cup_{n\in\N\cup\{0\}}\phi_n:T_3\map X$ with the required property. Therefore, we can take $K_{\ref{thm-emb of T3}}=K'$.
