As an application of Theorem \ref{main thm over ray graph gen} and Corollary \ref{cor-exponential growth QI inv}, we have the following.	

	\begin{cor}\label{cor-one fixed fiber}
		Suppose $\pi:X\map[0,\infty)$ is an $f$-metric graph bundle such that the fibers are uniformly quasiisometric to a fixed hyperbolic metric graph, say $Z$. Further, suppose that the fibers have uniformly bounded valence. Moreover, we assume that $Z$ has exponential growth. Finally, let $X$ be hyperbolic. Then the CT map $\pa\pi^{-1}(0)\map\pa X$ is surjective.
	\end{cor}
\begin{proof}
Since $Z$ has exponential growth and the fibers are quasiisometric to $Z$, by the first part of Corollary \ref{cor-exponential growth QI inv}, the fibers have exponential growth. On the other hand, the fibers have uniformly bounded valence and are uniformly quasiisometric to $Z$, by moreover part of Corollary \ref{cor-exponential growth QI inv}, the collection $\{F_i:i\in\N\cup\{0\}\}$ have uniform exponential growth. Then Corollary \ref{cor-one fixed fiber} follows from Theorem \ref{main thm over ray graph gen}.
\end{proof}

\subsection{Proof of Theorem \ref{thm-combo1} $(A)$ and Corollary \ref{cor-main group over ray}}\label{applications over ray sec} As an application of Theorem \ref{main thm over ray graph gen} and Corollary \ref{cor-one fixed fiber}, we will prove Theorem \ref{thm-combo1} $(A)$ and Corollary \ref{cor-main group over ray} respectively. We first prove Theorem \ref{thm-combo1} $(A)$ and then Corollary \ref{cor-main group over ray}.\smallskip

\noindent{\bf Proof of Theorem \ref{thm-combo1} $(A)$}: Note that we have some non-negative constants $\dl$, $L$ and $D$, and an $f$-metric graph bundle  $\pi:X\map[0,\infty)$ satisfying the following.



\begin{enumerate}
\item The fibers $F_i,~i\in\N\cup\{0\}$ and the total space $X$ are $\dl$-hyperbolic.

\item The barycenter maps $\pa^3F_i\map F_i$ are $L$-coarsely surjective.

\item Moreover, the valence at each vertex of $F_i$ in $F_i$ is bounded by $D$.
\end{enumerate}

\noindent Then by Theorem \ref{thm-bary imp expo growth}, each fiber has exponential growth, and moreover, the parameters of the exponential growth depend only on $\dl$ and $L$. Hence the collection $\{F_i:i\in\N\cup\{0\}\}$ have uniform exponential growth. Note that $X$ is hyperbolic and the fibers have uniformly bounded valence. Therefore, Theorem \ref{thm-combo1} $(A)$ follows from Theorem \ref{main thm over ray graph gen}.\qed\smallskip

\noindent{\bf Proof of Corollary \ref{cor-main group over ray}}: Let $G$ be a nonelementary hyperbolic group. We fix a finite generating set for $G$. Let $\Gamma_G$ be the Cayley graph with respect to this generating set. Note that by Theorem \ref{thm-exp growth rate hyp grp}, $\Gamma_G$ has exponential growth. Note that the fibers have uniformly bounded valence (assumption of Corollary \ref{cor-main group over ray}). Therefore, Corollary \ref{cor-main group over ray} follows from Corollary \ref{cor-one fixed fiber}.\qed\smallskip

