	We conclude this section with the following questions. Recall that in Theorem \ref{main thm over ray graph gen}, the assumption of uniform bounded valence of the fibers plays a crucial role in our argument. If this condition is relaxed, our argument no longer works. This motivates the following question.

	\begin{question}\label{qsn-general}
		Suppose $\pi:X\map[0,\infty)$ is an $f$-metric graph bundle with controlled hyperbolic fibers. Further, suppose that the fibers are proper metric spaces and are uniformly quasiisometric to a fixed hyperbolic space. Finally, assume that $X$ is hyperbolic. Is the CT map $\pa\pi^{-1}(0)\map\pa X$ {\em always} surjective?
	\end{question}

	\begin{remark}
