\noindent{\em Under the condition $(A)$}: Let $u\in V(B)$ and $F_u=\pi^{-1}(u)$. Let $x\in V(F_u)$. Then by Lemma \ref{lem-st pro imp st pro}, the valence at $x$ in $F_u$ is bounded by $N(4,1/3)$. This is true for any vertices $u\in V(B)$ and $x\in V(F_u)$.

