\section{Conclusion and Future Work}
\label{sec:conclusion}

In this paper, we introduced \texttt{PACE.jl}, a comprehensive Julia package that implements computational tools for solving various problems in control theory.
We illustrated the applicability of our tools through three examples in control theory, where, by using certified algorithms, we produced results that are guaranteed to be correct. 
Future work will focus on extending the package's functionality to handle more general classes of systems and control problems, 
as well as conducting comprehensive performance evaluations. In particular, we plan to implement methods for parametric 
$H_\infty$-norm computation using discriminant varieties, as proposed in \citep{Quadrat_Rouillier_Younes_2024}. 

